<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The M key's mark: the TSUNAGI///M slash motif.

  The app is TSUNAGI///Manifold (operator, 2026-10-20) and `///` is the brand's
  own motif — not one of the seven M ICON function words, which name categories
  (tsunagi-m-release §3.2). The M key is not a category: it is the door to all
  of them, so it carries the brand rather than any one of its rooms.

  What was here before was the owner's stepped-M glyph, traced from their master
  art. It was correct when the M key was the only brand surface on the console;
  it is superseded now that the product itself is named with the slashes.

  ## Geometry

  Identical to ic_launcher.xml's motif — `M2,30 L8,30 L16,2 L10,2 Z` and its two
  siblings on a 32-unit canvas — scaled by 0.75 to this 24-unit viewport and
  shifted 0.75 left so the ink is centred. The source runs x 2..32, drawn hard
  against its own right edge, and a mark that sits off-centre inside a 160x56
  key reads as a mark that was placed carelessly.

  This is the same path data the TUNER key carried until 2026-10-28, when that
  key took the `mapping` mark (docs/04 §10.14). The bars have not changed; they
  have stopped standing for one tool and gone back to standing for the family.

  Ink spans 22.5 x 21 of the viewport, so at d_m_logo_w = 22px the mark is about
  20.6 x 19.25 px — the stepped M it replaces was 20.54 x 20. The key's
  composition does not move.

  ## White, not the tricolour

  The source motif is ///M blue, indigo and red. Reproducing it here would put
  #F11A22 on a key face that runs #CE1533 to #920A21: the red stripe would
  disappear into the red. docs/04 §10.6 records exactly this failure for the
  logo navy on the old TUNER key — an invisible stripe is not a faithful mark,
  it is a two-bar mark.

  Hard-coded white rather than @color/d_icon because Face.BRAND is the one face
  ConsoleKeys.applyNight does not touch: the M key keeps its colour at night, so
  this mark has no night variant to stay in step with.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M0.75 22.5 H5.25 L11.25 1.5 H6.75 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M6.75 22.5 H11.25 L17.25 1.5 H12.75 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M12.75 22.5 H17.25 L23.25 1.5 H18.75 Z" />
</vector>
